  "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tAfrican-Language Data Quality\n\t\n\nSeven datasets built around one question: how do you tell good African-language text\nfrom bad, when there is no reference translation to compare against? They fall into\nthree families, which do not share a schema — load them by config name.\n\n\t\n\t\t\nconfig\nrows\nlanguages\nwhat it is\n\n\n\t\t\ndefault\n493,831\n71\nhuman text, corrupted by a known function by a known amount\n\n\n270m_inlang_full\n57,465\n71\nmodel-generated text, in-language prompts\n\n\n270m_inlang_b\n45… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/AletheiaAING/Data-Quality.",
